152
00:11:34,023 --> 00:11:39,023
くだらない 線 だな そのまま ああ
Such meaningless lines, just as they are, ah

153
00:11:39,023 --> 00:11:43,523
切って貼った皮 裂いて見えた痣
The skin that's cut and pasted, the bruises seen when torn

154
00:11:44,023 --> 00:11:49,023
ララ ラン ラララ 笑う ように 浮いた アバラ
La la lan lalala, floating ribs that seem to laugh

155
00:11:50,023 --> 00:11:54,023
ぎゅっ て 抱い た 空 だって 泣い た から
I held the emptiness tight, because I had cried

156
00:11:54,023 --> 00:11:59,023
ララ ラン ラララ なげく 壁 に 描い た パブロー・ピカソ
La la lan lalala, painted on the grieving wall — Pablo Picasso

157
00:12:00,023 --> 00:12:03,523
なぜか わたしの こと だなって 眺めちゃったよ
Somehow I found myself thinking "this is about me", as I gazed

158
00:12:03,523 --> 00:12:07,523
これが欲しいなって感じたの セザンヌの絵をキボンヌ なんてね
It made me feel "I want this" / Like "I wanna seize a Cézanne!", just kidding

159
00:12:07,523 --> 00:12:10,523
老人がとなりでじっと見てたよ
An old man beside me was staring

160
00:12:11,023 --> 00:12:15,523
欺瞞 ウソ 若さ ならば 本物の意味あるのかな
Deception and lies — if it's youth / I wonder if there's any meaning to the real thing

161
00:12:15,523 --> 00:12:20,523
真実抱いたまま 腐り落ちて床で死んでた
Whilst holding the truth in your arms, it rotted away and died on the floor

162
00:12:20,523 --> 00:12:25,523
赤 ずっと 塗り 込ん だ やっぱ ずっと 良かった
I kept plastering red all over — that was the best after all

163
00:12:26,023 --> 00:12:30,523
イヤ らしい 線 だな 今 もう ああ
Such nasty lines, even now, ah

164
00:12:42,523 --> 00:12:47,023
切って貼った皮 咲いて散った花
The skin that's cut and pasted, the flowers bloomed and scattered

165
00:12:48,023 --> 00:12:52,523
ララ ラン ラララ 笑う ように 見えた カラダ
La la lan lalala, a body that seems to laugh

166
00:12:53,023 --> 00:12:57,023
ぎゅっ て 抱い た 空 だって 泣い た から
I held the emptiness tight, because I had cried

167
00:12:58,023 --> 00:13:02,523
ララ ラン ラララ なげく 壁 に 描い た パブロー・ピカソ
La la lan lalala, painted on the grieving wall — Pablo Picasso

168
00:13:03,023 --> 00:13:06,023
わたし ウソ の ピカソ
I, the Picasso of lies

169
00:13:18,523 --> 00:13:20,523
やっと来た。
Finally.

170
00:13:20,523 --> 00:13:23,523
こんな不気味な場所で待たせないでほしいんだけど。
This is a creepy place to make someone wait.

171
00:13:23,523 --> 00:13:27,523
現場を調べたらKFPの近くに寄るから、店の近くで待っててって言ったのに。
I told you I'd come to the nearby KFP after investigating the crime scene.

172
00:13:28,023 --> 00:13:29,323
そんなの無理！
Not a chance!

173
00:13:29,323 --> 00:13:33,423
アンタと話すだけでもイヤなのに、話してるところを人に見られたらそれこそ最悪。
It's bad enough I have to talk to you. I don't want others to be around to see it.

174
00:13:33,423 --> 00:13:36,823
そんなアンタが手を貸してくれるなんて意外だけどね。
I'm surprised you're willing to cooperate in the first place.

175
00:13:37,023 --> 00:13:41,523
それは…例の殺人事件以降、いろいろ妙なことが起こってるの。
Yeah, well, ever since the murder, weird things have been happening.

176
00:13:41,523 --> 00:13:45,523
アンタが解決してくれるなら、こうやって会うのもやむなしよ。
I figure if you can help solve it, then it's worth the trouble of meeting with you.

177
00:13:45,523 --> 00:13:47,023
イヤだけど。
Just barely.

178
00:13:47,523 --> 00:13:48,523
妙なことが起こってる？
What weirdness?

179
00:13:49,023 --> 00:13:53,323
「人の形をした黒い影が見えた」って報告が、うちの従業員からちょくちょく出てるの。
Some of my employees have been complaining about seeing a shadowy figure.

180
00:13:53,523 --> 00:13:58,523
話によれば、最初は夢の中にそれが現れたんだけど、今は起きてる時も見えてるって――
They say it started with bad dreams, but now some are seeing it even when they're—

181
00:14:09,023 --> 00:14:10,023
アーニャ！
Anya!

182
00:14:11,023 --> 00:14:16,023
だ…大丈夫。それより…
I'm... fine, don't worry about me.

183
00:14:17,023 --> 00:14:18,223
これ見て。
Look at this.

184
00:14:18,223 --> 00:14:23,523
まったくもう、アンタはいつも大げさすぎ…ん？
Hmph. Course. You're just always being overly dramatic... huh?

185
00:14:24,023 --> 00:14:28,523
おかしいな。現場の証拠品は警察が全部回収したはずなのに。
Weird. I figured the cops would have already collected all the evidence.

186
00:14:29,023 --> 00:14:32,523
この近くに住んでるKFPの従業員で、被害者のことを知ってる者は？
Did any of your employees who live nearby know the victim?

187
00:14:32,523 --> 00:14:33,523
いない。
Nope.

188
00:14:34,023 --> 00:14:36,323
分かった。新しい情報が入ったらまた教えて。
Alright. Let me know if you hear anything else.

189
00:14:36,323 --> 00:14:37,523
ちょっと待った！
Wait!

190
00:14:37,523 --> 00:14:40,523
それだけ？私の時間を奪っておいてタダで帰るつもり？
That's it? You're not even gonna compensate me for my time?

191
00:14:41,023 --> 00:14:44,223
従業員のためかと思いきや、結局カネかい。
I thought you were doing this to help your employees.

192
00:14:44,223 --> 00:14:46,023
タダ働きはしない主義なの。
I'm still a businesswoman.

193
00:14:46,023 --> 00:14:51,323
いま持ち合わせがないんだけど、代わりに歌で支払うっていうのはどう？
Well, I don't have any cash on me, but I can pay you in song.

194
00:14:51,523 --> 00:14:55,523
ウソでしょ？歌うの？アンタと？
Seriously? You think I'd want to sing? With you?

195
00:14:56,023 --> 00:14:57,223
イナは歌で喜んでくれたけどなー。
Ina accepted payment in song.

196
00:14:57,223 --> 00:14:59,823
ただ、イナと歌うのは楽しいけど、
But then, singing with her is fun.

197
00:15:00,071 --> 00:15:01,071
...is fun.

198
00:15:01,071 --> 00:15:02,171
With you...

199
00:15:02,271 --> 00:15:03,171
With me, what?

200
00:15:03,271 --> 00:15:04,971
You don't think I'm good enough for you?!

201
00:15:05,071 --> 00:15:07,071
Let's go, punk! You and me, right now!

202
00:15:13,771 --> 00:15:15,871
全部全部あんたのせいだ
It's all, all your fault

203
00:15:15,871 --> 00:15:17,871
反吐が出るくらいにウザったいわ
So annoying, it makes me want to throw up

204
00:15:17,871 --> 00:15:19,871
何かにすがってへつらって
Clinging to something and flattering

205
00:15:19,871 --> 00:15:21,871
期待したアタシが馬鹿だった
I was a fool to have expected anything

206
00:15:21,871 --> 00:15:23,971
ご機嫌伺いのアパシー
Toadying apathy

207
00:15:23,971 --> 00:15:25,971
それ故にアンチな一生ギミー
And thus, give me a lifetime of hate

208
00:15:25,971 --> 00:15:27,971
浅いキャパシティ毎度おおきに
Shallow capacity, thanks as always

209
00:15:27,971 --> 00:15:29,871
詰まるとこ人生ずっと地味
In short, my life is always plain

210
00:15:29,871 --> 00:15:31,971
「憎らしい！」 「痛々しい！」
“Detestable!” “Pathetic!”

211
00:15:31,971 --> 00:15:33,871
無視出来ないのが一層腹立たしい
The fact that I can't ignore it is even more irritating

212
00:15:33,871 --> 00:15:35,871
苛立たしい そろそろ飽きた自画自賛に
Frustrating, I'm getting tired of your self-praise

213
00:15:35,871 --> 00:15:37,971
ライクの反対はアパシー
The opposite of 'like' is apathy

214
00:15:37,971 --> 00:15:39,971
イコールで繋がれた証
A proof of being connected with an equals sign

215
00:15:39,971 --> 00:15:41,971
切り離せない関係
An inseparable relationship

216
00:15:41,971 --> 00:15:43,971
逸らしてしまいたいわ
I just want to look away

217
00:15:43,971 --> 00:15:45,971
これは所謂ヘイトスピーチ
This is a so-called hate speech

218
00:15:45,971 --> 00:15:51,071
匿名性の声明を生命に乗せてんだ
Carrying an anonymous statement on my life

219
00:15:51,071 --> 00:15:53,071
鳴り止まないサイレン 近づく度、痙攣
Unceasing siren, convulsing every time it gets closer

220
00:15:53,071 --> 00:15:55,071
赤信号にずっと従順です
Always obedient to the red light

221
00:15:56,571 --> 00:15:58,071
ねえ
Hey...

222
00:15:58,071 --> 00:16:00,071
大体アナタのコト アタシ
Mostly, when it comes to you, I...

223
00:16:00,071 --> 00:16:02,071
ダイダイダイダイダイキライ
Hate, hate, hate, hate, hate you!

224
00:16:02,071 --> 00:16:04,071
omg 情けない 最早
OMG, how miserable, already

225
00:16:04,071 --> 00:16:06,071
バイバイバイバイバイしたい
I want to say bye-bye-bye-bye-bye!

226
00:16:06,071 --> 00:16:07,871
脳内も予測不能故に
Since even inside my brain is unpredictable

227
00:16:07,871 --> 00:16:09,871
解解解 解は無い
Solve, solve, solve, there is no solution

228
00:16:09,871 --> 00:16:11,871
どうだい？アタシのことアナタ
How about it? Do you...

229
00:16:11,871 --> 00:16:13,871
ダイダイダイダイダイキライになった？
Hate, hate, hate, hate, hate me now?

230
00:16:13,871 --> 00:16:17,071
あぁ百害あって一利ナシ nothing not see
Ah, a hundred harms and not a single benefit, nothing, not see

231
00:16:17,071 --> 00:16:21,071
もしタラレバ並べてもニコチンだし
Even if we talk about 'what ifs', it's just nicotine

232
00:16:21,071 --> 00:16:24,071
i miss you って近付いた結末は凡ミス 凡ミス
The ending that approached saying 'I miss you' is a simple mistake, simple mistake

233
00:16:24,071 --> 00:16:28,071
センキュー反面教師 後味一生消えてくんないわ
Thank you, bad example, the aftertaste won't disappear for a lifetime

234
00:16:29,071 --> 00:16:31,071
よしよし いい子ね
There, there, good girl

235
00:16:31,071 --> 00:16:33,071
笑顔振り撒き パラパラ いい子ね
Scattering smiles, flutter, flutter, good girl

236
00:16:33,071 --> 00:16:35,071
だけど だけど その本性は？
But, but, what is her true nature?

237
00:16:35,071 --> 00:16:37,071
善悪の区別も付かないの？はぁ
Can't you even tell right from wrong? Sigh...

238
00:16:37,071 --> 00:16:39,071
減点方式で取り巻く環境に巻かれて
Wrapped in an environment that surrounds with a demerit system

239
00:16:39,071 --> 00:16:42,071
生涯、痛い！痛い！痛い！も聞こえないわ！って
In my lifetime, 'It hurts! It hurts! It hurts!' won't even be heard!

240
00:16:42,071 --> 00:16:44,071
当然の報いにクラっちゃった
Hit by the natural retribution

241
00:16:59,071 --> 00:17:01,071
人は鏡なんです
People are mirrors

242
00:17:01,071 --> 00:17:03,071
実のところ依存は両辺です
To tell the truth, dependence is mutual

243
00:17:03,071 --> 00:17:05,071
シャットダウンしても付き纏う
Even if you shut down, it follows you around

244
00:17:05,071 --> 00:17:07,071
己の弱さが不甲斐ない
My own weakness is disappointing

245
00:17:07,071 --> 00:17:09,071
全部全部あんたのせいって
It's all, all your fault

246
00:17:09,071 --> 00:17:11,071
反吐が出るくらいに止まんないわ
So much that I want to throw up, it won't stop

247
00:17:11,071 --> 00:17:14,071
いっその事 切り離した方が楽なのにね
Even though it would be easier to just cut you off

248
00:17:15,571 --> 00:17:17,571
大体アナタのコト アタシ
Mostly, when it comes to you, I...

249
00:17:17,571 --> 00:17:20,071
ダイダイダイダイダイキライ
Hate, hate, hate, hate, hate you!

250
00:17:20,071 --> 00:17:22,071
omg 情けない 最早
OMG, how miserable, already

251
00:17:22,071 --> 00:17:24,071
バイバイバイバイバイしたい
I want to say bye-bye-bye-bye-bye!

252
00:17:24,071 --> 00:17:25,871
脳内も予測不能故に
Since even inside my brain is unpredictable

253
00:17:25,871 --> 00:17:27,871
解解解 解は無い
Solve, solve, solve, there is no solution

254
00:17:27,871 --> 00:17:29,871
どうだい？アタシのことアナタ
How about it? Do you...

255
00:17:29,871 --> 00:17:31,071
ダイダイダイダイダイキライになった？
Hate, hate, hate, hate, hate me now?

256
00:17:31,071 --> 00:17:34,071
あぁ百害あって一利ナシ nothing not see
Ah, a hundred harms and not a single benefit, nothing, not see

257
00:17:34,071 --> 00:17:38,071
もしタラレバ並べてもニコチンだし
Even if we talk about 'what ifs', it's just nicotine

258
00:17:38,071 --> 00:17:41,071
i miss you って近付いた結末は凡ミス 凡ミス
The ending that approached saying 'I miss you' is a simple mistake, simple mistake

259
00:17:41,071 --> 00:17:45,071
センキュー反面教師 後味一生消えてくんないわ
Thank you, bad example, the aftertaste won't disappear for a lifetime

260
00:18:11,871 --> 00:18:14,371
はぁ、もう、誰なの？
Sigh, who is it now?

261
00:18:14,371 --> 00:18:15,571
はーい。
Come in.

262
00:18:16,271 --> 00:18:18,271
アーニャ、ヤッホー。
Hey, Anya! Ya doing okay?

263
00:18:19,071 --> 00:18:21,071
って、大丈夫そう？
Wait, are you okay?

264
00:18:21,071 --> 00:18:23,971
なんか顔色悪いね。
You look kind of... not great.

265
00:18:24,071 --> 00:18:27,071
大丈夫...じゃないかもね。
Thanks... maybe not.

266
00:18:27,071 --> 00:18:29,871
ちょっと横になった方がいいんじゃない？
You just need sleep!

267
00:18:29,871 --> 00:18:33,871
周りをぐるぐる走ってあげるから、わための数を数えるといいよ。
Lie down, and I'll run in circles so you can count me~

268
00:18:34,071 --> 00:18:36,071
心配かけてごめん。
Sorry, but not now.

269
00:18:36,071 --> 00:18:38,271
でも今寝たらダメなんだ。
I can't go to sleep right now.

270
00:18:38,271 --> 00:18:42,571
なぜならあと、もうちょっとでこの事件を解決できそうなんだから！
I'm close to cracking this case wide open!

271
00:18:42,571 --> 00:18:43,871
そう？
You sure?

272
00:18:43,871 --> 00:18:45,871
そうかも、そうじゃないかも。
I don't know! Yes? Maybe?

273
00:18:45,871 --> 00:18:50,071
わかんないけど、とりあえずヒントは揃ったんだ。
I do have all the hints...

274
00:18:50,071 --> 00:18:53,071
ほな、難しいか。
That doesn't seem very sure...

275
00:18:53,071 --> 00:18:57,271
わため先輩、程々にしておきましょう。
Watame-senpai, I think you're annoying her.

276
00:18:57,571 --> 00:19:01,071
わためは悪くないよねぇー！
Watame did nothing wrong.

277
00:19:01,071 --> 00:19:05,071
これが事件を解く鍵なんだ。探偵の直感がそう言ってる。
This is an important clue! I can feel it in my gut,

278
00:19:05,071 --> 00:19:08,871
でもDNA鑑定では何もわからなかった。
but a DNA trace was a dead end.

279
00:19:08,871 --> 00:19:13,571
じゃあ、これは何なんだ？！これは何なんだ？！
So what does it mean? What does it mean?!

280
00:19:13,571 --> 00:19:16,871
その布でそんなにお困りなら...
That it's a mean cloth? If you're that troubled...

281
00:19:16,871 --> 00:19:19,871
あ、じゃあ、わためが食べてあげる！
Oh! I could eat it.

282
00:19:20,571 --> 00:19:24,071
ねえ、アーニャ、それちょっと見せてくれる？
Hey Anya? Can I take a look at that?

283
00:19:31,071 --> 00:19:35,571
この布についてわかったことはあるけど...
If I tell you something about this cloth,

284
00:19:35,571 --> 00:19:41,271
それを教えたら、ちょっと休憩しない？
will you agree to take a break?

285
00:19:41,271 --> 00:19:46,071
一旦仕事の手は止めて、私たちと遊ぼうよ。
Maybe do something fun with us before you go back to work?

286
00:19:46,071 --> 00:19:49,071
じゃあ一緒に歌でも歌う？
We could sing together.

287
00:19:49,071 --> 00:19:52,271
この街では情報は歌で買うものみたいだし。
That seems to be the going rate for information around here.

288
00:19:52,271 --> 00:19:54,071
おお、楽しそう！
Oh, that sounds fun!

289
00:19:54,071 --> 00:19:59,071
おっけー。その布には魔力の痕跡を感じるんだ。
Alright... I can sense a magical residue on this cloth.

290
00:20:01,346 --> 00:20:02,546
そんなバカな
That can't be true.

291
00:20:03,446 --> 00:20:06,346
忘れたの？アイリスはネフィリム。
Hey, I'm a nephilim, remember?

292
00:20:06,746 --> 00:20:09,546
魔力を感じとるなんてお手の物。
We get a bonus to detect magic!

293
00:20:10,546 --> 00:20:14,646
あれ？アーニャもこの布が怪しいと思ってたんじゃないの？
Wait... you already had your suspicions about the cloth, didn't you?

294
00:20:15,346 --> 00:20:17,546
そうだけどさー。
Yeeaaah... but...

295
00:20:17,546 --> 00:20:22,046
でも殺人事件と超常現象なんて、混ぜたらだめなやつでしょ？
but supernatural stuff happening in a murder case? They're not supposed to mix.

296
00:20:22,646 --> 00:20:25,846
そう？でもそういうアニメとかドラマも…
Really? But in some shows—

297
00:20:26,246 --> 00:20:29,046
まあまあ、物騒な話はそのくらいにして。
Enough murder talk.

298
00:20:29,046 --> 00:20:31,546
みんなで歌っちゃおう！
Let's sing~

299
00:20:48,346 --> 00:20:50,046
この路地を抜けろ awake now
Get through this alley, awake now

300
00:20:54,046 --> 00:20:56,546
僕ら 覚醒 アップデート ey
We awaken, update, ey

301
00:20:58,346 --> 00:21:01,046
ギラギラ 光らせた
Make it shine brilliantly

302
00:21:01,446 --> 00:21:04,546
いいな いいな そのカラット
So nice, so nice, that carat

303
00:21:05,146 --> 00:21:08,546
目立っちゃうな 自然に 視線を 独り占め
Standing out, naturally monopolizing all eyes

304
00:21:08,946 --> 00:21:11,846
この手口は盗めない
This technique can't be stolen

305
00:21:12,346 --> 00:21:15,846
答えなら「好きなだけ」が極まってく
If it's an answer, "as much as you like" reaches its peak

306
00:21:17,446 --> 00:21:20,546
一秒前完全アップデート ya ya
One second ago, a complete update, ya ya

307
00:21:21,046 --> 00:21:24,046
不安グッバイ 自分以外は敵じゃない
Anxiety, goodbye, no one but myself is the enemy

308
00:21:24,046 --> 00:21:27,546
お利口御無用指を立てろ
No need to be a good kid, raise your finger

309
00:21:28,046 --> 00:21:31,046
ha～ 揺れろ 運命
ha~ Shake, destiny

310
00:21:31,546 --> 00:21:34,546
ah～ あたしらしいウルトラ C
ah~ Ultra C, just like me

311
00:21:34,946 --> 00:21:39,046
その感情を燃料に持ち込む延長戦へ全能
With that emotion as fuel, carrying our all-power into extra time

312
00:21:39,046 --> 00:21:42,546
嗚呼、体が
Ah, my body...

313
00:21:42,546 --> 00:21:45,046
この生き様で make some noise
Make some noise with this way of life

314
00:21:45,046 --> 00:21:48,546
見舞う we gotta go メディカルボイス
We gotta go pay a visit, medical voice

315
00:21:48,546 --> 00:21:53,046
宿した熱狂は伝播する 真っ向から着弾
The passion we harbor spreads, hitting right on target

316
00:21:53,046 --> 00:21:56,046
もらうわ大歓声
I'll take the huge cheers

317
00:21:57,046 --> 00:21:59,046
what i want to touch down

318
00:22:00,046 --> 00:22:03,546
燃やせ 革命 アップデート hey
Burn, revolution, update hey

319
00:22:08,546 --> 00:22:11,546
僕が覚醒、逆転 ey
I awaken, reversal, ey

320
00:22:12,746 --> 00:22:16,546
ひとりきりじゃ just kidding
Just kidding on my own

321
00:22:16,546 --> 00:22:20,046
君とだから dreaming
Because I'm with you, dreaming

322
00:22:20,146 --> 00:22:24,046
間違いだらけ 勘違いもしてときめきをリテイク
Full of mistakes, even misunderstanding, retake that heartbeat

323
00:22:27,546 --> 00:22:30,046
ey 失っても尚 コンティニュー
ey, even if I lose, still continue

324
00:22:30,046 --> 00:22:33,546
支払った代償の自分 あの日に…してないわけない後悔
The self that paid the price, there's no way I don't regret that day...

325
00:22:35,046 --> 00:22:37,046
胸に飾れ
Decorate your chest

326
00:22:37,046 --> 00:22:38,546
前向き直せ 唱えて
Turn forward, fix it, recite it

327
00:22:38,546 --> 00:22:41,546
（諦め悪いって？）信じてくれ
("Hard to give up?") Believe in me

328
00:22:50,046 --> 00:22:53,046
青く燃ゆる 僕は炎
Burning blue, I am a flame

329
00:22:53,046 --> 00:22:57,046
時は経てど 恋うは心
Time passes, but the heart still yearns

330
00:22:57,046 --> 00:23:00,046
誰だ 誰だ 誰だ あたしだ さあお任せ
Who is it, who is it, who is it? It's me, leave it to me

331
00:23:07,046 --> 00:23:10,046
この生き様で make some noise
Make some noise with this way of life

332
00:23:10,046 --> 00:23:11,546
有終の美 get up! hey, raise the bro
Graceful end, get up! hey, raise the bro

333
00:23:11,546 --> 00:23:14,046
宿した逆境に下克上 とうとう役満
Rebellion against the hardship, finally a grand slam

334
00:23:14,046 --> 00:23:17,546
あげるわ 大団円
I'll give you a grand finale

335
00:23:20,546 --> 00:23:22,546
what i want to touch down

336
00:23:23,046 --> 00:23:25,546
燃やせ 革命 アップデート hey
Burn, revolution, update hey

337
00:23:28,046 --> 00:23:30,046
go all out

338
00:23:33,046 --> 00:23:35,546
僕が覚醒、逆転 ey
I awaken, reversal, ey

339
00:23:57,546 --> 00:24:01,546
以上がこちらで調べた情報です。いかがですか？
So that's everything I've got so far. What do you think?

340
00:24:01,546 --> 00:24:03,546
と、ここで、大空警察。
And so, here she visits the Oozora Police.

341
00:24:04,046 --> 00:24:08,046
数々の難事件を解決してきた。
With their stellar track record of solving mysterious cases easily...

342
00:24:08,046 --> 00:24:12,546
優秀な警察から、今回の事件に関するさらなる情報を得るべく、
in hopes of getting more information regarding this case from the excellent police force,

343
00:24:12,546 --> 00:24:16,846
探偵は、警察署を訪れていた。
the detective visited the police station.

344
00:24:17,146 --> 00:24:22,046
はっからー！事件の捜査は我々プロに任せておけばいいんだよ！
Oh, please! You should leave the investigation to us, the professionals!

345
00:24:26,546 --> 00:24:31,046
何？被害者の服に魔力の痕跡があったって？
What? Magical residue was found on the victim's clothing?

346
00:24:31,546 --> 00:24:34,546
そうだ！そんなバカな話があるか！
Exactly! How could such an absurd story be true?

347
00:24:35,046 --> 00:24:42,546
こいつ、次、自分自身が凶器かもしれないとか言い出すんじゃないですか？署長。
Next, she's probably going to tell us that she herself might be the murder weapon, right, Chief?

348
00:24:52,546 --> 00:24:54,046
それだ！
Wait, that's it!

349
00:24:54,046 --> 00:24:55,546
はぁ？
Huh?

350
00:24:56,046 --> 00:25:00,046
こいつ今、自分が凶器だって自白した？
Did she just confess to being the murder weapon?

351
00:25:00,094 --> 00:25:03,494
よく分かんないっす。ボクが言ったのはただの冗談で...
I'm not sure. I was just joking about that... unless...

352
00:25:03,494 --> 00:25:08,794
もしかしてボク、無意識のうちに真実をつかんでいたのか！？
What if I subconsciously knew the truth this whole time!

353
00:25:08,794 --> 00:25:10,594
お前天才か！？
You are a genius!

354
00:25:10,594 --> 00:25:16,694
おや、これはいよいよ事件解決・・になってしまうのか？
Oh my, could this possibly mean... the case is solved?

355
00:25:16,694 --> 00:25:18,794
事件解決しちゃった！
I solved the case!

356
00:25:18,794 --> 00:25:23,594
違う違う。私は凶器じゃないですよ。
I'm not the murder weapon.

357
00:25:23,594 --> 00:25:27,094
異議あり！さっき自白しただろ！
OBJECTION! You already confessed!

358
00:25:27,094 --> 00:25:33,594
私が言いたいのは、この事件にはまた別の古代兵器が関わっているかもしれないということ。
What I mean is, maybe there was another ancient weapon involved.

359
00:25:33,594 --> 00:25:36,594
だから布に魔力が残っていたんだ。
That would explain the magical residue on the cloth.

360
00:25:36,594 --> 00:25:40,594
なんだそういうことか…
I guess that makes sense.

361
00:25:40,594 --> 00:25:44,794
僕が事件を解決できたと思ったのに…
But I wanted to solve the case...

362
00:25:44,794 --> 00:25:47,094
まあ次がんばれよ。
You will solve the next one.

363
00:25:47,094 --> 00:25:53,594
でもなぁ、現場の近くで変なものを見たっていう報告も届いてるんだ。
But we've also gotten reports of people seeing strange things near the murder scene.

364
00:25:53,594 --> 00:26:05,094
その魔力の痕跡とやらが超常的な力によるものだっていうなら、変な幻覚が見えた人がいるのもそいつの影響ってこと？
If the involvement of something supernatural explains the magical residue, does it also cover those weird visions?

365
00:26:05,094 --> 00:26:09,594
それはまだ分かりませんが、謎は必ず解いてみせましょう。
I'm not sure yet, but I'm going to find out.

366
00:26:09,594 --> 00:26:13,094
じゃあうちの捜査資料を持って行っていいよ。
Then we will give you our case file to help out.

367
00:26:13,094 --> 00:26:15,594
民間人にあげちゃダメっすよ！
You can't give that to a civilian!

368
00:26:15,594 --> 00:26:19,094
でもこいつさぁ、なんか天才の匂いしね？
But she seems like a genius.

369
00:26:19,094 --> 00:26:23,094
さっきはボクのこと天才って言ったじゃないですかぁ・・。
But you said I was a genius just a moment ago...

370
00:26:23,094 --> 00:26:25,094
どんな情報でも助かりますよ。
Any information you have would be useful.

371
00:26:25,094 --> 00:26:32,594
ただし！資料が欲しいなら、タダというわけにはいかんな！
Fiiine! But if you want our files, then we need something in return.

372
00:26:32,594 --> 00:26:37,094
これ、また歌う流れですか？
Could that thing be, perhaps, a song?

373
00:26:43,594 --> 00:26:46,594
おれは知らない 何も知らない
I don't know, I don't know anything.

374
00:26:46,594 --> 00:26:50,094
何も見てない 誰も見てない
I didn't see anything, nobody saw anything.

375
00:26:50,594 --> 00:26:54,094
空を見ても 見えない 夜の
Even if I look up at the sky, I can't see the night's...

376
00:26:54,094 --> 00:26:57,594
欠けた月に 兎
...rabbit on the waning moon.

377
00:26:57,594 --> 00:27:01,094
これはなんだ それが何か？
What is this? What is that anyway?

378
00:27:01,094 --> 00:27:04,894
ここは楽し それでよろし
It's fun here, so that's good enough.

379
00:27:04,894 --> 00:27:08,094
走る 逃げる 逃がす 逸らす
Run, flee, let go, look away,

380
00:27:08,094 --> 00:27:11,894
月の欠けた場所へ
...to where the moon has waned.

381
00:27:11,894 --> 00:27:26,094
あらら あらら あらら あらら あらら あらら
Oh dear, oh dear, oh dear...

382
00:27:26,094 --> 00:27:29,594
妄想 止め処なく
Unstoppable delusions,

383
00:27:29,594 --> 00:27:33,094
創造 咎めなく
...unreproached creations,

384
00:27:33,094 --> 00:27:36,594
衝動 収まらず
...uncontrollable impulses.

385
00:27:36,594 --> 00:27:40,594
なぜか なぜか なぜか なぜかしら
Why, why, why, I wonder why?

386
00:27:40,594 --> 00:27:44,294
最悪だ！公序良俗を剥いで脱いで踊れ！
This is the worst! Strip away public order and morals and dance!

387
00:27:44,294 --> 00:27:48,094
いや最低か！なんでなんでつって なんかなんか高鳴って
Or are you the lowest? Asking why, why, my heart is somehow pounding.

388
00:27:48,094 --> 00:27:51,594
最悪だ！どうもこうもしねぇよ勝手にしやがれ！
This is the worst! There's nothing to be done, do whatever you want!

389
00:27:51,594 --> 00:27:55,094
いや最低か！いやーもうほんと 最悪だ！だ！だ！だ！だ！
Or are you the lowest? No, seriously, it's the absolute worst!

390
00:27:55,094 --> 00:27:58,594
ねてもさめてもつきまとう
Haunting me whether awake or asleep,

391
00:27:58,594 --> 00:28:02,094
みえぬいしきのうらがわに
...behind my unseen consciousness,

392
00:28:02,094 --> 00:28:05,594
おおきくあいたくろいあな
...a gaping black hole.

393
00:28:05,594 --> 00:28:09,094
わかる わかる わかる
I understand, I understand, I understand.

394
00:28:09,094 --> 00:28:12,594
許す 許せん 許す 許せん
Forgive, unforgivable, forgive, unforgivable.

395
00:28:12,594 --> 00:28:15,594
かわいい えへへ むふふ こわい
Cute, hehe, mufu, scary.

396
00:28:15,594 --> 00:28:19,094
りんご ごりら らくご ごじら
Apple, Gorilla, Rakugo, Godzilla,

397
00:28:19,094 --> 00:28:22,594
らっぱ だぶら らまだ
Trumpet, Double, Ramada.

398
00:28:37,594 --> 00:28:41,094
私たち絶対に見てません
We definitely didn't see anything!

399
00:28:41,094 --> 00:28:44,594
言ってもせん 聞いてもせん 知ったこっちゃありません
We didn't say, we didn't hear, we don't care at all!

400
00:28:44,594 --> 00:28:48,094
光を失し 影に一粒
Losing the light, a single drop in the shadow,

401
00:28:48,094 --> 00:28:51,094
許されざる思考を
...an unforgivable thought.

402
00:28:51,094 --> 00:28:53,094
当てはまらない異常を
With an abnormal state that doesn't fit in,

403
00:28:53,094 --> 00:28:56,594
包んで生きていこうじゃありませんか
...why don't we wrap it up and keep on living?

404
00:28:56,594 --> 00:28:59,894
葛藤 名も持たず
Conflict without a name,

405
00:28:59,894 --> 00:29:03,094
狂騒 意味もなく
...frenzy without a meaning,

406
00:29:03,094 --> 00:29:06,594
栄光 自己満足
...glory of self-satisfaction.

407
00:29:06,594 --> 00:29:10,594
だから だから だからなんなのさ
So, so, so what about it?

408
00:29:10,594 --> 00:29:14,294
最高だ！脳が凌駕してんだ ぶっ壊して叫べ！
This is the worst! My brain is overriding everything, break it and scream!

409
00:29:14,294 --> 00:29:18,094
いや最高か！なんでなんでつって 舞いも舞いも跳ねちゃって
Or is it the best? Asking why, why, dancing and leaping around.

410
00:29:18,094 --> 00:29:21,594
最高だ！降起降起で結構 勝手に生きたれ！
This is the worst! Rise up, rise up, it's fine, live however you want!

411
00:29:21,594 --> 00:29:25,094
いや最高か！いやーもうほんと 最高だ！だ！だ！だ！だ！
Or is it the best? No, seriously, it's the absolute best!

412
00:29:25,094 --> 00:29:28,594
むかしむかしのおもいづき
A whim from once upon a time,

413
00:29:28,594 --> 00:29:32,094
むいみむいみのひとだかり
...a meaningless crowd of people,

414
00:29:32,094 --> 00:29:35,594
むじゃきむてきのうまれつき
...innocent and invincible by nature.

415
00:29:35,594 --> 00:29:39,094
それが それが それが
That is, that is, that is...

416
00:29:39,094 --> 00:29:43,094
無責任に集合体
An irresponsible collective,

417
00:29:43,094 --> 00:29:46,594
あんたも私も関係ない
...it has nothing to do with you or me.

418
00:29:46,594 --> 00:29:50,094
無責任に集合体
An irresponsible collective,

419
00:29:50,094 --> 00:29:53,594
楽しくやってりゃもう満開
...if we're having fun, we're in full bloom.

420
00:29:53,594 --> 00:29:55,594
勝手にやってりゃ問題無し
If we do whatever we want, there's no problem.

421
00:29:55,594 --> 00:29:58,594
おれは知らない 何も知らない
I don't know, I don't know anything.

422
00:29:58,594 --> 00:30:00,094
何も見てない 何も見てない
I didn't see anything, nothing...

423
00:30:00,569 --> 00:30:01,269
辛い
Painful...

424
00:30:01,269 --> 00:30:02,069
疑問
Questions...

425
00:30:02,069 --> 00:30:03,069
違い
Differences...

426
00:30:03,069 --> 00:30:04,269
夢の話
Talks of dreams...

427
00:30:04,269 --> 00:30:05,569
そういうこと？
Is that so?

428
00:30:05,569 --> 00:30:07,569
それじゃ、
Well then...

429
00:30:15,569 --> 00:30:20,569
超常的な力が殺人事件に関わっている？
A supernatural occurrence, happening in a murder case?

430
00:30:20,569 --> 00:30:24,569
いやいやそんな、ねえ？
That's just unbelievable, right?

431
00:30:24,569 --> 00:30:31,069
にわかには信じがたいが、今の手がかりから推理するとそういうことになる。
She had a hard time believing it, but all the hints said otherwise.

432
00:30:31,069 --> 00:30:37,069
まだパズルのピースがピタリとはまらないこの不思議で奇妙な事件。
Still, there were pieces of this puzzle that refused to fit, this strange and bizarre case.

433
00:30:37,069 --> 00:30:43,069
探偵は信頼できる情報源に頼ることにした。
So the detective turned to a reliable source for help.

434
00:30:43,269 --> 00:30:45,369
あっ、来てくれたー
Ah, you came-

435
00:30:45,369 --> 00:30:49,069
...なんで君達まで？
...And why are you guys also here?

436
00:30:49,569 --> 00:30:53,069
ゼータが来るって聞いたから、アーニャにちょっかいかけてやろうと思って！
We heard Zeta was coming over, and decided to bug ya!

437
00:30:53,069 --> 00:30:54,869
はいはい。
Yes, yes, I see.

438
00:30:54,869 --> 00:30:56,869
もー！つれないなぁ。
Aww, come on!

439
00:30:56,869 --> 00:30:59,069
それはそうと...ゼータ、何か掴めた？
Anyway, Zeta, did you find anything?

440
00:30:59,069 --> 00:31:03,569
もちろん！優秀なシークレットエージェントなので！
Of course! I'm not an elite secret agent for nothing!

441
00:31:03,569 --> 00:31:11,069
イナの描いた似顔絵と大空警察の資料から、被害者の身元を特定できたよ。
Between the portrait from Ina and the files from the Oozora Police, I've been able to positively ID the murder victim.

442
00:31:11,069 --> 00:31:14,069
でも...ちょっと変なんだよね。
But... what I found is weird.

443
00:31:14,069 --> 00:31:15,069
変？
How so?

444
00:31:15,069 --> 00:31:20,069
被害者の履歴を調べたところ、その人物は何百年も前の時代の人だったんだ。
Well, when I investigated their history, I found that they actually lived centuries ago.

445
00:31:20,069 --> 00:31:25,869
でもその人物が、数日前に死体で発見された...話がつながらないよ。
So how they were also somehow murdered just days ago... it doesn't make any sense.

446
00:31:25,869 --> 00:31:29,869
アーニャからもらった情報に間違いがあったとか？
Did you perhaps confuse your information? Or...

447
00:31:29,869 --> 00:31:34,569
なるほど、やっとつながってきた。
Actually, things are finally starting to make sense.

448
00:31:34,569 --> 00:31:37,569
一人の被害者が、過去と現在で二度死んだことになる。
A victim caught between two times.

449
00:31:37,569 --> 00:31:40,569
誰かが時間と次元をねじ曲げて、そんな状況を作り出した。
One who died in two different ways.

450
00:31:40,569 --> 00:31:46,569
なかなかできることじゃない...
Not many exist who can cause time and dimensions to warp in a way to make that possible...

451
00:31:46,569 --> 00:31:49,069
でも君なら可能でしょ。
...but you're one of them.

452
00:31:49,069 --> 00:31:52,569
さすがは名探偵。
Well done, detective.

453
00:31:52,569 --> 00:31:57,069
ちょっと時間がかかりすぎかな。危うくネタばらしするとこだった。
Took you long enough. I was this close to telling ya the whole thing.

454
00:31:57,069 --> 00:32:00,069
レイネが書いてくれた、この匿名の手紙もいいヒントになったよ。
You helped enough with this "anonymous" letter about the murder.

455
00:32:00,069 --> 00:32:02,569
えっ、バレてた？
O-oh, you figured out that was me?

456
00:32:02,569 --> 00:32:04,569
書き方のクセで分かる。
I recognized your writing style.

457
00:32:04,569 --> 00:32:09,569
待って、どういうこと？ムーナと被害者にどんな関係があるの？
W-wait, I don't get it. What does Moona have to do with the victim?

458
00:32:09,569 --> 00:32:14,869
ムーナは、別の時空で殺された遺体を我々がいるこの時空へ移動させたんだ。
She took a murder victim from another space and time, and moved them into our dimension.

459
00:32:14,869 --> 00:32:18,869
ゼータが特定した人物は、この世界線における同じ人物ってこと。
The one you ID'ed was this universe's version of the same person.

460
00:32:18,869 --> 00:32:23,869
なるほど...？でもどうしてそんなことを？
Uh... okay. But then why?

461
00:32:23,869 --> 00:32:30,069
理由も気になるけど、それより確かめたいことがある。
That is an important question, but there's one I want answered even more.

462
00:32:30,069 --> 00:32:33,869
ムーナが...私にあの夢を見せたの？
Are you... responsible for my dreams?

463
00:32:33,869 --> 00:32:35,269
それは違う。
No.

464
00:32:35,269 --> 00:32:41,069
あなたがあの夢を見ていることを知って、私はあの夢が生まれる根源を調べてみた。
After I learned about your dreams, I used my powers to search for the source of them.

465
00:32:41,069 --> 00:32:45,069
そして見つけたのが、次元の向こう側から声を届けようとする魂。
I found a spirit reaching out from time and dimensions.

466
00:32:45,069 --> 00:32:49,069
私はその魂のために橋渡しをしてあげただけ...
All I've done is try to help them by making the bridge a little easier...

467
00:32:49,069 --> 00:32:52,569
私も手伝ったよ！というか、私のアイデア。
With my help! I mean, it was my idea...

468
00:32:52,569 --> 00:32:55,069
そう。
True.

469
00:32:55,069 --> 00:33:00,569
ただやり方が悪かったのか、アーニャの見たものが他の人にも見えちゃったみたい。
Though doing it this way has caused some of what you've been experiencing to leak to other people.

470
00:33:00,569 --> 00:33:04,569
巻き込んだKFPの従業員には後でお詫びしなきゃ...
We're going to have to apologize to the KFP workers...

471
00:33:04,569 --> 00:33:08,569
でもその魂が、どうして私に声を届けようとしてるの？
But why is the spirit reaching out to me of all people?

472
00:33:08,569 --> 00:33:13,569
それは私に訊くことじゃないね。私が話すべきことじゃない。
It wouldn't be right for me to answer those questions. It's not my story to tell.

473
00:33:13,569 --> 00:33:17,869
あの魂に心を開いてあげて。それだけでいい。
Open yourself up to the spirits, and they'll do the rest.

474
00:33:17,869 --> 00:33:20,569
心をもっと開く方法なら知ってるよ！
I got a way to make yourself more open to spirits!

475
00:33:20,569 --> 00:33:22,869
それって歌？
Is it through song?

476
00:33:22,869 --> 00:33:24,569
え？なんで分かったの？
Huh? How'd you know?

477
00:33:24,569 --> 00:33:27,569
まあ、勘かな...
Lucky guess...

478
00:33:55,069 --> 00:33:59,569
思い返していた 思い出の中で泣いていた
I was looking back, crying inside my memories.

479
00:33:59,569 --> 00:34:05,069
不確かな夢と語録を掛け合って笑った
We laughed, multiplying our uncertain dreams and quotes.

480
00:34:05,069 --> 00:34:10,569
この旅路も奇数も絶えないと 瞳を見返してスマイル仕様な
Hoping this journey and these odd moments won't end, I look back into your eyes and put on a smile.

481
00:34:10,569 --> 00:34:16,069
焦りと不安が滲んで涙に呑まれてしまう
Impatience and anxiety seep in, and I end up swallowed by tears.

482
00:34:16,069 --> 00:34:21,069
誰一人 欠けることはないチームはぐなっつ
Not a single person will be missing, Team Hagnuts.

483
00:34:21,069 --> 00:34:26,569
僕らの思いが音になって繋ぐ
Our feelings turn into sound and connect us.

484
00:34:26,569 --> 00:34:32,569
こだまして 忘れないよ 隠した秘密を
Echoing, I won't forget the secrets we hid.

485
00:34:32,569 --> 00:34:36,569
あの日僕らは間違っていなかったんだと知る
Knowing that on that day, we weren't wrong.

486
00:34:36,569 --> 00:34:42,569
閉ざして しまい込んだ 一線の光探して
Searching for a beam of light shut away and locked inside.

487
00:34:42,569 --> 00:34:45,569
君の声を聞かせて
Let me hear your voice.

488
00:34:45,569 --> 00:34:48,869
ここにいるって叫んでくれよ
Shout out that you are here!

489
00:34:48,869 --> 00:34:54,069
その手を離さないで
Don't let go of that hand.

490
00:34:54,069 --> 00:35:00,069
世界に僕だけ取り残されてしまう
Or I'll end up left behind all alone in this world.

491
00:35:00,117 --> 00:35:01,117
...られたかな
...I could have lived easier.

492
00:35:01,617 --> 00:35:06,617
暗闇の中で 立ち止まり 手放してしまう
Stopping in the darkness, I end up letting go.

493
00:35:07,117 --> 00:35:11,917
心が通じ合えない 孤独感を 押し殺してしまうなら
If I must suppress this loneliness of not being understood...

494
00:35:11,917 --> 00:35:16,917
1人でいた方が 楽に生きられたかな
...maybe it would've been easier to live alone.

495
00:35:17,417 --> 00:35:18,917
憧れ
Longing...

496
00:35:18,917 --> 00:35:22,617
理想に強く惹かれる感情が
These emotions strongly drawn to ideals...

497
00:35:22,617 --> 00:35:26,617
僕らを引き寄せてしまうのなら
...if they draw us together...

498
00:35:26,617 --> 00:35:30,117
応えて
Answer me.

499
00:35:37,617 --> 00:35:39,617
くらまして
Dazzle me,

500
00:35:39,617 --> 00:35:44,917
まだ終わっちゃいないんだ僕ら 延長戦だろう
We aren't done yet, this is extra time.

501
00:35:44,917 --> 00:35:49,117
この音が途切れるまで
Until this sound completely fades out.

502
00:35:49,117 --> 00:35:53,617
子供の頃に描いたヒーロー
The hero I imagined in my childhood...

503
00:35:53,917 --> 00:35:57,617
君の出番が待ってる
...your turn is waiting.

504
00:35:58,617 --> 00:36:00,117
くらまして
Dazzle me,

505
00:36:00,117 --> 00:36:03,617
忘れないようかき鳴らした日々を
The days we played so we wouldn't forget...

506
00:36:03,617 --> 00:36:08,617
あの日の僕らは間違っていなかったんだと知る
...letting us know we weren't wrong back then.

507
00:36:09,117 --> 00:36:11,917
閉ざしてしまいこんだ
Locked away...

508
00:36:11,917 --> 00:36:14,917
一閃の光探して
...searching for a flash of light.

509
00:36:14,917 --> 00:36:18,117
君の声を聞かせて
Let me hear your voice.

510
00:36:18,117 --> 00:36:21,917
ここにいるって叫んでくれよ
Scream out that you're right here.

511
00:36:21,917 --> 00:36:27,617
その手を離さないで
Don't let go of my hand.

512
00:36:38,917 --> 00:36:43,617
魂に心を開け？簡単に言ってくれる。
Opening up to the spirit? That was a tall order.

513
00:36:44,617 --> 00:36:53,617
探偵になる前の彼女の人生において、他者に心を開くのは危険な行為だった。
In her life before being a detective, opening up to someone was dangerous.

514
00:36:54,117 --> 00:36:57,117
今でもその本能は変わらない。
That instinct still lingers.

515
00:36:59,917 --> 00:37:02,617
結局何も進展はなかった。
This was getting her nowhere.

516
00:37:02,617 --> 00:37:09,617
謎はまだ残っているが、彼女はここのところ無理が続いていた。
She still had questions she needed answered, but maybe she had wound herself up too much.

517
00:37:13,617 --> 00:37:16,317
少し休まなければ。
She needed a break.

518
00:37:24,617 --> 00:37:27,617
Hello everyone! I'm Hatsune Miku, a virtual idol!

519
00:37:27,617 --> 00:37:33,317
Well, that's what everyone seems to think... But secretly I'm a detective!

520
00:37:33,617 --> 00:37:36,917
ええ？ミクちゃん？！
Eeh? Miku-chan?!

521
00:37:37,117 --> 00:37:39,117
あ、アーニャちゃん！
Ah, Anya-chan!

522
00:37:39,117 --> 00:37:41,617
一緒に歌おう！
Let's sing together!

523
00:37:41,617 --> 00:37:44,317
わあー！
Wow!

524
00:37:44,317 --> 00:37:46,917
I wake up to a call, put my frilly outfit on now

525
00:37:46,917 --> 00:37:49,317
It's time I open up my eyes and start the day

526
00:37:49,317 --> 00:37:51,917
I combat till the dawn, until every villain's gone, wah!

527
00:37:51,917 --> 00:37:54,517
A clumsy trip and now I've fallen to my butt

528
00:37:54,517 --> 00:37:59,117
With my magical phone and a silly little ringtone

529
00:37:59,117 --> 00:38:01,617
I'll shout a magic word and set the world in place

530
00:38:01,617 --> 00:38:04,617
Whatever it may cost, there's no reason to stop for a world that I cherish and love

531
00:38:04,617 --> 00:38:09,117
Monsters might be a scary foe to fight, but I'll take the stand if I can stop your tears and wipe them dry

532
00:38:09,117 --> 00:38:13,617
If my pain's a type of cure for peace, I don't mind, I can play as a nurse healing you everyday

533
00:38:13,617 --> 00:38:19,617
So what if I might shed a tear, get some bruises? A wipe is all I need to clean the cherry blush away, ha!

534
00:38:19,617 --> 00:38:22,117
Fighting through the night, but I'm wide awake

535
00:38:22,117 --> 00:38:24,617
It can all be so hard for me to get through the day

536
00:38:24,617 --> 00:38:27,117
Your smile is enough to heal all my aches

537
00:38:27,117 --> 00:38:29,617
Wrapped in a cute band-aid, I can take the pain

538
00:38:29,617 --> 00:38:31,617
Fight all day

539
00:38:31,617 --> 00:38:34,117
Fill up the syringe with love, heal up the world and go again

540
00:38:40,117 --> 00:38:44,317
Ur yaoi! Ur yaoi! Oooo fighter! Super powerful Miku-chan!

541
00:38:44,317 --> 00:38:49,117
Ur yaoi! Ur yaoi! Oooo cyber! Miku Miku Miku go!

542
00:38:49,117 --> 00:38:54,117
And now, it's time for the moment you've been waiting for!

543
00:38:54,117 --> 00:38:58,617
1! 2! 3! Ready?! Miku Miku beam!

544
00:39:09,117 --> 00:39:12,117
On my own without anyone to know

545
00:39:12,117 --> 00:39:14,617
How my job's not all rainbows

546
00:39:14,617 --> 00:39:19,617
But then I think about your smile

547
00:39:19,617 --> 00:39:24,117
I'm a magically bright invincible girl! If you need me to heal, go on and call out my name

548
00:39:24,117 --> 00:39:29,117
When you find yourself going down a spiral, I'll bonk away what puts you down, a pink hammer melee! Yah!

549
00:39:29,117 --> 00:39:31,617
Fighting through the night, but I'm wide awake

550
00:39:31,617 --> 00:39:34,117
All alone it's so hard for me to get through the rain

551
00:39:34,117 --> 00:39:36,617
Your smile is enough to make my day

552
00:39:36,617 --> 00:39:39,117
So I stand tall and brave 'cause I'm not afraid

553
00:39:39,117 --> 00:39:41,117
Any pain I can laugh away

554
00:39:41,117 --> 00:39:44,117
Chin up with love, I'll fight on till the end

555
00:39:44,117 --> 00:39:49,117
Bearing through the pain, I'll try to be brave, as long as you can stay happy, I'm okay

556
00:39:55,117 --> 00:39:58,117
あ、あ、眠いよ〜
Ah, I'm so sleepy...

557
00:40:04,892 --> 00:40:06,892
I wake up to a call

558
00:40:06,892 --> 00:40:08,892
put my frilly outfit on now

559
00:40:08,892 --> 00:40:11,892
It's time I open up my eyes and start the day

560
00:40:11,892 --> 00:40:13,892
I combat till the dawn

561
00:40:13,892 --> 00:40:15,892
until every villain's gone, wah!

562
00:40:15,892 --> 00:40:18,892
A clumsy trip and now I've fallen to my butt

563
00:40:18,892 --> 00:40:20,892
With my magical phone

564
00:40:20,892 --> 00:40:22,892
and a silly little ringtone,

565
00:40:22,892 --> 00:40:24,892
I'll shout a magic word

566
00:40:24,892 --> 00:40:26,892
and set the world in place

567
00:40:26,892 --> 00:40:28,892
Whatever it may cost, there's no reason to stop,

568
00:40:28,892 --> 00:40:30,892
for a world that I cherish and love

569
00:40:30,892 --> 00:40:32,892
Oya oya oya oya, oh, fight on!

570
00:40:32,892 --> 00:40:35,592
Super power, power of love, make a magic charge!

571
00:40:35,592 --> 00:40:37,592
Oya oya oya oya, oh, fight on!

572
00:40:37,592 --> 00:40:39,592
Miku miku miku miku go!

573
00:40:40,892 --> 00:40:43,092
あー、眠いよ。
Ah, I'm so sleepy.

574
00:41:00,892 --> 00:41:03,892
夢だった？！
It was a dream?!

575
00:42:51,592 --> 00:42:53,092
知った
I knew...

576
00:42:53,092 --> 00:42:58,592
救いのない形だった 僕の
...it was a helpless form, my...

577
00:42:58,592 --> 00:43:00,292
知った
I knew...

578
00:43:00,292 --> 00:43:05,292
狂いのない赤い血が 流れているんだ
...that error-free red blood is flowing inside me.

579
00:43:05,292 --> 00:43:08,892
ただただ遅い来る影ばかり 目に満ちて
Only shadows attacking me fill my eyes,

580
00:43:08,892 --> 00:43:12,092
からかう言葉 立ち上がれないような風
teasing words, a wind that won't let me stand up.

581
00:43:12,092 --> 00:43:14,292
赤く光る地平へ
To the glowing red horizon,

582
00:43:14,292 --> 00:43:17,292
裸足で駆けだしたら
if I start running barefoot,

583
00:43:17,292 --> 00:43:19,892
ただ膝を抱えている君がいたから
you were there, just holding your knees.

584
00:43:19,892 --> 00:43:20,892
だから
And so...

585
00:43:20,892 --> 00:43:24,092
ENCOUNT 悲劇ぶった天国へ
Encountering toward a tragic heaven,

586
00:43:26,292 --> 00:43:29,592
不甲斐ない瞳切ったあの日
on that day I cut my helpless eyes.

587
00:43:29,592 --> 00:43:32,892
見つめた君のせい
It's because of you whom I stared at.

588
00:43:32,892 --> 00:43:38,892
早く 早く 早く 早く 早く 早く 早く 早く
Hurry, hurry, hurry, hurry, hurry, hurry, hurry, hurry...

589
00:43:38,892 --> 00:43:40,892
身を委ねて
surrender yourself.

590
00:45:01,940 --> 00:45:05,140
奪い合う瞳 幾度
Eyes vying with each other, how many times...

591
00:45:05,140 --> 00:45:08,140
崩れた貴方望む
have I wished for your broken self?

592
00:45:08,140 --> 00:45:09,640
I can't wait to watch you lose it.

593
00:45:09,640 --> 00:45:10,940
rotten, falling down

594
00:45:10,940 --> 00:45:15,140
はやく はやく ねぇ教えて
Quickly, quickly... Hey, tell me?

595
00:45:15,140 --> 00:45:20,640
調教 樹海 秘密のむこうへと
Training, a sea of trees, to the beyond of secrets.

596
00:45:21,140 --> 00:45:23,140
SIX SENSE OOPARTS
Sixth sense, OOPArts.

597
00:45:29,640 --> 00:45:33,140
不甲斐ない 瞳 きっとあの日
Those useless eyes... Surely, on that day...

598
00:45:33,140 --> 00:45:35,940
みつめた 貴方のせいだ
it's because of you, who I gazed at.

599
00:45:35,940 --> 00:45:41,640
はやく はやく
Quickly, quickly...

600
00:45:41,640 --> 00:45:44,340
はやく息を止めて
Quickly hold your breath,

601
00:45:44,340 --> 00:45:49,140
淡い淡い水面のむこうへと
to the beyond of the pale, pale water's surface.

602
00:45:50,340 --> 00:45:53,440
白い光をみつめていると
When I gaze at the white light,

603
00:45:53,440 --> 00:45:56,940
急な痛みに襲われる
I'm overcome by sudden pain.

604
00:45:56,940 --> 00:46:01,940
僕は私を保っていられなくなること
Knowing I will no longer be able to maintain my self...

605
00:46:01,940 --> 00:46:06,640
それをこの小さな器が証明している
this small vessel proves exactly that.

606
00:46:06,640 --> 00:46:10,640
はじめに、安堵するきみがみたい
First, I want to see you relieved.

607
00:46:10,640 --> 00:46:14,640
つぎに、期待したい
Next, I want to hope.

608
00:46:34,140 --> 00:46:37,640
この場所で戦いなど起こっていない。
There was no major battle here.

609
00:46:38,140 --> 00:46:41,640
少なくともこの世界線では...
At least not in this timeline...

610
00:46:43,140 --> 00:46:50,640
だが探偵には分かっていた。彼女が見たものは決して夢ではないことを。
But the detective knows what she saw was no dream.

611
00:46:51,640 --> 00:46:56,640
心の中にはまだ殺戮の匂いが漂っている。
The smell of the carnage still lingers in her mind.

612
00:46:57,640 --> 00:47:03,640
かつての彼女にまとわりついていた、あの匂い。
It's a scent that was, at one time, so familiar to her.

613
00:47:04,640 --> 00:47:15,640
探偵としての生活も今では順調だが、そうでなければあの匂いからは離れることができなかったでしょう。
That stench would still linger on her if the detective's life didn't take a turn for the better.

614
00:47:16,640 --> 00:47:22,640
今でも... あの頃の日々がリアルな夢のようにまとわりつく。
Even now... her days felt more like the real dream.

615
00:47:23,640 --> 00:47:27,140
終わるべくして終わったおとぎ話。
A fairytale. Maybe one that deserved to end.

616
00:47:27,640 --> 00:47:35,640
どこまで行っても彼女は、生まれ持った本質から逃れることはできない。
Because, at the end of the day, she can never run away from her nature.

617
00:47:39,640 --> 00:47:44,640
それでも今は違う。今の彼女には仲間がいる。
But she's not just that anymore. She has friends to thank for that.

618
00:47:45,140 --> 00:47:50,640
それが、別の世界線の彼女とは違う点なのかもしれない。
Maybe that was what separated her from the other version.

619
00:47:52,640 --> 00:48:00,640
もしかしたらあの子は、幸せに生きることのできた世界線があったのだろうかと、
And, maybe... that version of herself just wanted a ray of hope,

620
00:48:01,140 --> 00:48:06,640
そんな一筋の希望を求めていたのだろうか。
to know that there was one timeline where things worked out.

621
00:48:07,140 --> 00:48:16,640
そしてその幸せな世界線というのは、ここではないまた別の世界線のことかもしれない...
Or perhaps this was never about the detective...

622
00:48:17,140 --> 00:48:22,640
考えが頭を巡るものの、答えが出ることはない。
so many thoughts run amok inside her head, but they're forever left unanswered.

623
00:48:24,140 --> 00:48:32,640
何にせよ、探偵は自身の血塗られた過去を忘れることはないでしょう。
Whatever the case, the detective won't forget her bloody past,

624
00:48:33,140 --> 00:48:36,640
しかしまた後戻りするつもりもない。
but she isn't going to revert to it either.

625
00:48:37,140 --> 00:48:43,140
彼女はこれからも仲間とともに進む。
She will continue to move forward with her friends,

626
00:48:43,640 --> 00:48:50,140
望んだ結末を迎えられなかった別の自分たちのためににも。
and for all the variants who didn't get their desired ending.

627
00:48:50,640 --> 00:48:53,940
探偵アーニャ・メルフィッサは、
The detective, Anya Melfissa,

628
00:48:54,140 --> 00:48:59,140
明日に向かって生き続ける。
will keep on living for her own tomorrow.

629
00:49:09,140 --> 00:49:16,640
Anya Melfissa Birthday Live 2024!

630
00:49:16,640 --> 00:49:20,140
How did everyone like it? Oh my goodness!

631
00:49:20,140 --> 00:49:26,640
やっと今年も参りました、アーニャの誕生日です！いかがでしたでしょうか？
Anya's birthday has finally come around again this year! How did you all like it?

632
00:49:27,140 --> 00:49:37,140
This time, I tried to incorporate a little bit of story into my 3D birthday celebration. And I think it turned out pretty nice, you know?

633
00:49:37,140 --> 00:49:44,140
You get story part and also live part, and I think it turned out pretty well!

634
00:49:44,140 --> 00:49:54,140
And also, how was my new original song? Oh my goodness! How was my new original song? It was good, wasn't it? I hope you all liked it!

635
00:49:54,140 --> 00:49:59,140
新曲もね、あの、歌わせていただきました。いかがでしたでしょうか？
I got to sing my new song too. How did you all like it?

636
00:50:00,115 --> 00:50:01,415
Ah! Oh my god!

637
00:50:01,415 --> 00:50:02,915
I celebrated...

638
00:50:02,915 --> 00:50:05,015
...um, I celebrated...

639
00:50:05,015 --> 00:50:07,515
...my birthday with...

640
00:50:07,515 --> 00:50:09,215
...a lot of friends too this year!

641
00:50:09,215 --> 00:50:10,115
Yeah!

642
00:50:10,115 --> 00:50:12,815
A lot of the girls came to celebrate my birthday.

643
00:50:12,815 --> 00:50:15,615
And also Detective Anya managed...

644
00:50:15,615 --> 00:50:18,115
...to solve that mission. Wow, she's got it!

645
00:50:18,115 --> 00:50:20,115
Detective Anya!

646
00:50:20,115 --> 00:50:23,115
Did you guys like Detective Anya as well?

647
00:50:23,115 --> 00:50:27,315
Detective Anya was pretty cool, but not as cool as me!

648
00:50:27,315 --> 00:50:30,515
Oh my god! And also, special guests!

649
00:50:30,515 --> 00:50:33,315
There were special guests!

650
00:50:33,315 --> 00:50:38,315
Oh my god, I can't believe I got to sing with Hatsune Miku!

651
00:50:38,315 --> 00:50:40,115
Hatsune Miku-chan!

652
00:50:40,115 --> 00:50:43,115
Oh my god, she was really cute!

653
00:50:43,115 --> 00:50:46,515
And also, for the narration for my story part...

654
00:50:46,515 --> 00:50:48,915
...Ueda Reina-san narrated!

655
